"""Original application assessment; open-book practice, not qualification acceptance."""
QUESTIONS=[]
def q(stem,options,answer,feedback): QUESTIONS.append(dict(question=stem,options=options,answer=answer,feedback=feedback))
q('A temperature alarm test passes. Which claim still needs separate evidence?',['The alarm responded in the tested condition','The test used the recorded configuration','The product blend is uniform throughout'],2,'A defined alarm response does not establish product mixing performance.')
q('A material finding remains open at IQ handover. What determines whether a proposed OQ activity can proceed?',['Documented impact and authorization for that activity','The proportion of installation rows already signed','Whether the supplier expects closure this week'],0,'Assess the specific next activity and obtain authorization; progress counts and promises do not establish readiness.')
q('A supplier protocol tests a different software configuration. What is needed before use?',['Use it unchanged if the model name matches','Review applicability and supplement or revise appropriately','Repeat only the tests that the supplier marked difficult'],1,'The site establishes suitability for its actual configuration and procedures before approval.')
q('A test has no defined response-time criterion. What is appropriate?',['Treat the first measured interval as the maximum','Use the fastest result from three repeated trials','Resolve the criterion through the controlled process'],2,'Acceptance cannot be invented from the result. Define and approve the test basis before deciding acceptance.')
q('An input occurs at 14:20:10.0 and the defined output at 14:20:13.2. What is the elapsed time?',['3.2 seconds','13.2 seconds','23.2 seconds'],0,'Subtract synchronized start and end times: 13.2 minus 10.0 equals 3.2 seconds. Clock suitability remains necessary.')
q('The intended range is inside the manufacturer design envelope. What does this establish by itself?',['Every setting in the range is qualified','Testing above the rating is justified','Only that it fits the stated design envelope'],2,'A design rating is not evidence of qualification coverage; tests and rationale are still needed.')
q('A plan requires all pairs of two loads and three speeds. How many combinations does that plan contain?',['Five combinations','Six combinations','Nine combinations'],1,'Two times three equals six. This is the stated teaching matrix, not a regulatory minimum number of tests.')
q('Which rationale best supports a selected low-load challenge?',['It targets an identified immersion or control risk','It is always more demanding than any high load','It avoids the need to justify omitted conditions'],0,'A low-load condition needs a mechanism-specific rationale; it is not universally worst case.')
q('An alarm annunciates, but the required output does not change. How should the combined requirement be evaluated?',['Pass because the controller detected the condition','Pass if the operator acknowledges the alarm','Fail and investigate the missing required response'],2,'The complete stated requirement includes the output response; annunciation alone is insufficient.')
q('A simulated transmitter signal is injected downstream of the sensing element. Which limitation should be stated?',['The sensor itself was not challenged by that simulation','The controller could not receive the simulated input','The test automatically includes final actuator movement'],0,'The injection boundary excludes upstream sensing; other observations determine whether the actuator was actually checked.')
q('The fictional design requires manual reset after a trip. What should recovery verification include?',['Only removal of the initiating condition','The specified reset and controlled restart behavior','Only the appearance of the normal display'],1,'Removing the fault and satisfying the required reset/restart sequence are distinct observations.')
q('An error is +0.4 °C against a simple ±0.5 °C limit. What is the limited conclusion?',['The measurement has zero uncertainty','Every uncertainty decision rule would accept it','The absolute error meets that simple comparison'],2,'The simple comparison passes, but uncertainty, method suitability and the prescribed decision rule remain relevant.')
q('A stated teaching rule requires absolute error plus expanded uncertainty ≤0.5 °C. Error is +0.4 °C and uncertainty 0.2 °C. What follows?',['Accept because 0.4 is smaller than 0.5','Do not accept: the rule gives 0.6 °C','Accept because 0.4 minus 0.2 is 0.2'],1,'0.4 + 0.2 = 0.6 °C, above 0.5 °C. This conservative illustrative rule is not a universal GMP formula.')
q('A control trend is satisfactory for one selected minute but unstable during the prescribed evaluation interval. What is defensible?',['Evaluate the complete prescribed interval and investigate','Report only the stable minute as representative operation','Average away the instability without retaining the trend'],0,'The predefined evaluation and complete original data govern interpretation; selective reporting hides relevant behavior.')
q('After a simulated interruption, the machine runs again but a setting is lost. What does this indicate?',['Recovery is acceptable because movement resumed','The lost setting matters only during installation','Recovery needs assessment against its full requirements'],2,'Running again does not establish correct retained configuration or data continuity.')
q('A report contains selected screenshots of a raw electronic trend. What should happen to the applicable original data?',['Discard it once the screenshots are approved','Retain it under defined controls and retention arrangements','Keep it only when the report includes a failed result'],1,'Summaries do not replace applicable original records. Retention depends on the record and applicable obligations.')
q('A logging gap occurs during a challenge. Which response preserves defensible evidence?',['Retain partial data, assess impact and justify any repeat','Fill the interval using the expected response curve','Replace the first record once a repeat is satisfactory'],0,'Preserve the original and document the gap, investigation and authorized continuation or repeat.')
q('A parameter correction is followed by a passing retest. Which statement is justified?',['The original configuration can now be reported as passing','All related functions are validated by the one repeat','The repeat supports only its defined post-change scope'],2,'Keep the original failure and assess wider impact; one passing repeat does not establish every related function.')
q('Eleven of twelve tests pass, with one protective-function failure. What does approximately 91.7% mean?',['A pass rate, not qualification acceptance','Automatic qualification because it exceeds 85%','A basis to remove the remaining requirement'],0,'11 divided by 12 is about 91.7%. The significance of the failed test remains; the course practice score is unrelated.')
q('OQ supports finalizing an operating and cleaning procedure. Which additional conclusion would be unsupported?',['The procedure can incorporate the observed operating limits','Cleaning effectiveness has therefore been validated','The PQ handover should identify configuration and restrictions'],1,'A finalized procedure alone does not establish validated cleaning effectiveness or product performance.')
